      "writtenOn": "2022-03-15T19:09:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Lukasz and Jakub,\nIt seems the client is taking the preferred QoS parameters from server. Since the spec defines sets of QoS paramters for low latency audio data and High Reliability audio data, it is open for balanced latency setting and QoS might varies a lot from device to device. Would client take antyhing from server in the balanced mode? How do you plan to solve the QoS conflict for multiple devices within the same group?\n\nAlso, QoS setting is based on codec configuation, and the codec specific parameter is optional from client per spec, and it is impossible for server to select QoS without codec configuration. Is there any default coedc config server should be based on to select QoS?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1159,
        "startChar": 66,
        "endLine": 1159,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "31c30dbba48fe7f9826e652306261bb9262e738c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d47ced23_36961ace",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/state_machine.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T12:49:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should be \"\u003e\" ?\n\nI have test device that would support maximum transport latency of 20ms, and maximum retransmission number of 5 for media streams.\nWith this patch applied, it fails to stream media, this fixes the issue",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1166,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 1166,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "31c30dbba48fe7f9826e652306261bb9262e738c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99fa45df_fa92fffe",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/state_machine.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1085519
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T13:01:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We intentionally want to allow peer device to ask for more re transmissions if it is needed. \n\nWhere is the issue? Is it controller or peer device issue?",
      "parentUuid": "d47ced23_36961ace",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1166,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 1166,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "31c30dbba48fe7f9826e652306261bb9262e738c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5f4bb87_2c736c7b",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/state_machine.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T13:08:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Remote wants to use what we have as QoS_Config_48_4_1\n\n        {\n            \"name\": \"QoS_Config_48_4_1\",\n            \"retransmission_number\": 5,\n            \"max_transport_latency\": 20\n        },\n        \nWe want to use latency of 100, retransmission of 13.\n\nLogic in line 1158 would negotiate latency to be 20, but retransmissions would stay at 13, which is incorrect configuration.\n\n\nIf  max transport latency matches QoS_Config_48_4_1, we should use retransmissions number from same QoS configuration.",
      "parentUuid": "99fa45df_fa92fffe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1166,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 1166,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "31c30dbba48fe7f9826e652306261bb9262e738c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bcc58299_64bdc81a",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/state_machine.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1085519
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T13:18:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually Jakub just double check speck and you are about right\nPreferred retransmission number is what we shall to use in the Config QoS as per specification.\n\n\"Server preferred value for the\nRetransmission_Number parameter to be written\nby the client for this ASE in the Config QoS\noperation defined in Section\"\n\n\nThis brings me to my first thinking, that we should stick only to the Target Latency.\n\nFor sure this part we need to remove or hide for testing only.",
      "parentUuid": "99fa45df_fa92fffe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1166,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 1166,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "31c30dbba48fe7f9826e652306261bb9262e738c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a902f461_51df81db",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/state_machine.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1929540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T14:38:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We had some internal discussion and we are not 100% sure if we should allow to force QoS configurations. Especially that what BAP spec provides are only values for Low latency and High Reliable. In fact remote always can come up with other parameters, and what is important is if controller accepts it.\n\nAnyway as for now, to fix our issue with test device please create additional qos_configuration:\n\n```\n{\n   \"name\": \"QoS_Config_Server_Preferred\",\n   \"retransmission_number\": 0,\n   \"max_transport_latency\": 0\n},\n```\n\nAnd also please create additional configuration with this new QoS and make them highier prio in set_scenarios.",
      "parentUuid": "bcc58299_64bdc81a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1166,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 1166,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "31c30dbba48fe7f9826e652306261bb9262e738c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd3d4b2e_b8470d29",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/state_machine.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1904217
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-03T17:18:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Lukasz, Jakub,\n\nIn order to address the issue Jakub was facing, Can you please check uploaded patch once?\n\nOur intention is to let the client/phone drive the QoS selection, as the client has the information on the ContextType and user\u0027s audio preference. In cases, where the client preference is not supported by the remote, we will fall back to remote preferred values.\n\nTable 4.3 (ASCS): \"Server preferred value for the Retransmission_Number parameter to be written by the client for this ASE in the Config QoS operation defined in Section 5.2.\". Our understanding of the spec is that this is just indicating the server\u0027s preferred value and not mandating that this value be used in Config QoS.",
      "parentUuid": "a902f461_51df81db",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1166,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 1166,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "31c30dbba48fe7f9826e652306261bb9262e738c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
